-- title:
--   Matrices in the hereditary subalgebra of a corner entry $E_{ii}(h)$ are supported in the $(i,i)$ corner
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a C*-algebra (not necessarily unital) and $n\in\mathbb{N}$. For $a\in A$ and indices $j,k\in\{1,\dots,n\}$ let $E_{jk}(a)\in M_n(A)$ be the matrix whose $(j,k)$ entry is $a$ and whose other entries are $0$. For an element $x$ of a C*-algebra $C$ write
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{Her}(x)=\overline{\{\,x\,c\,x^{*} : c\in C\,\}}
--   $$
--
--   for the norm closure of $xCx^*$; it is a closed $*$-subalgebra of $C$ (for positive $x$, the hereditary C*-subalgebra generated by $x$).
--
--   **Theorem.** Let $i\in\{1,\dots,n\}$ and $h\in A$, and let $a\in M_n(A)$ belong to $\operatorname{Her}(E_{ii}(h))$, computed in the C*-algebra $M_n(A)$. Then for all $j,k\in\{1,\dots,n\}$:
--   1. $a_{jk}\in\operatorname{Her}(h)$ (computed in $A$);
--   2. $a_{jk}=0$ whenever $j\neq i$ or $k\neq i$.
--
--   In other words, $\operatorname{Her}(E_{ii}(h))\subseteq\{E_{ii}(b) : b\in\operatorname{Her}(h)\}$.
--
--   This lets one read off scalar information from matrix computations: whenever a construction in $M_n(A)$ lands in the hereditary subalgebra of a single corner $E_{ii}(v)$, its only possibly nonzero entry is the $(i,i)$ entry, and that entry lies in $\operatorname{Her}(v)$. It is used to extract orthogonal families of maps into $A$ from transports constructed at the matrix level.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Indices run over `Fin n`; $E_{jk}(a)$ is `entry j k a` (built from `Matrix.single`), and `Her x` is the topological closure of the $*$-subalgebra whose carrier is $\{x c x^*\}$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/CStarAlgebra/PureInfiniteness/OrthogonalSlots.lean#L125-L152

